# The authority that published this deployment's ladder presets. Without it
# the app labels every config as third-party and never offers to create one.
# `bun run configs:init` prints the value to use.
VITE_TAPER_ADMIN=

# The endpoint each network ships with. Pool and position browsing is
# getProgramAccounts, which the public endpoints rate-limit per IP, so a busy
# page hits 429 part way through a list and looks broken.
#
# Whatever goes here is baked into the JS bundle and is public to anyone who
# opens the app, so a paid endpoint put here is a shared quota with a key you
# can only revoke by rotating. A visitor can point their own browser at their
# own endpoint from the RPC chip in the header, which is stored locally and
# needs no rebuild.
#
# `bun run dev` proxies the devnet and mainnet endpoints through the Vite
# server (`/rpc/devnet`, `/rpc/mainnet`) instead of letting the page call them
# cross-origin, so an endpoint that mishandles the CORS preflight still works
# locally and its key never enters the dev bundle. A production build has no
# proxy: check that a deployed endpoint answers OPTIONS with
# `access-control-allow-origin` before shipping it here.

# Mainnet is hidden from the network picker until this is set. That is not a
# guard — the program has the same address everywhere and anyone may point a
# browser at it — it is because the public mainnet endpoint refuses this app's
# getProgramAccounts, so offering mainnet without an endpoint offers a page
# that cannot list a pool.
VITE_MAINNET_RPC=

VITE_DEVNET_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com
VITE_LOCALNET_RPC=http://127.0.0.1:8899
